the prior does not seem very sharp to me:

> f = function(x) 2*exp(x)/(1+exp(x))-1
> summary(f(rnorm(1000, mean=3, sd = 2/sqrt(10))))
     Min.   1st Qu.    Median      Mean   3rd Qu.      Max.
0.7409497 0.8868188 0.9064026 0.9026668 0.9252006 0.9657134

you might want to change the mean and prec to get something you like.

if you use the the rw1 as the model for the group, then there is
no sum-to-zero constraint in it.

let me know...
