the control.link is like a control statement for the link for the family which
'control.family' define, and is given inside, like this...

control.family = list(...,
control.link = list(model = "test1",
hyper = list(theta = list(
prior = "..",
param = "..."))))

some link functions can and will have unknown parmeters, but most will not.

> - `control.predictor(link = 1)`: determines the index of the family which should use for computing the posterior of the distribution

yes, its a vector, but the special case lenght() = 1, then we replicate it with the length of the data.

